ct of nutritional education, highlighting its importance in disease prevention and health maintenance.\",4\r\n953,COMISIÓN EUROPEA,\"The Comisión Europea, also known as the European Commission, is the executive body of the European Union. It plays a crucial role in proposing legislation and implementing decisions within the EU framework. Recently, the Comisión Europea presented a report to the European Parliament and Council concerning foods intended for athletes. Additionally, it is responsible for ensuring that food labeling regulations are updated and enforced, highlighting its commitment to maintaining food safety and transparency in the market.\",10\r\n863,PARLAMENTO EUROPEO,\"The Parlamento Europeo, or European Parliament, is a key legislative institution within the European Union responsible for defining and regulating food hygiene standards across the region. It establishes necessary measures to ensure the safety of food products, thereby protecting consumer health. Additionally, the European Parliament has adopted regulations concerning food labeling, which aim to provide consumers with essential information about the products they purchase. Furthermore, the Parlamento Europeo has engaged with reports from the Comisión Europea, specifically regarding foods targeted at athletes, highlighting its role in addressing various aspects of food regulation and consumer protection within the EU.\",4\r\n7785,DRI,Dietary Reference Intakes (DRI) are a set of reference values designed to plan and assess nutrient intakes for healthy individuals. These guidelines encompass recommendations for nutrient intake aimed at promoting health and preventing chronic diseases.,3\r\n7794,EU,\"The European Union (EU) is a political and economic union of member states primarily located in Europe. It plays a significant role in regulating food standards, including those specifically for athlete-targeted products. Additionally, the EU provides dietary recommendations for sodium intake and is actively working on harmonizing food labeling legislation across its member states.\",5\r\n14387,CCAH,\"The Comisión de Alimentación Humana (CCAH) is an organization dedicated to promoting health and nutrition, particularly in the context of athletic performance. CCAH advocates for specific guidelines concerning isotonic beverages, focusing on their osmolality to ensure optimal hydration and energy replenishment for athletes. Additionally, the organization has drafted a comprehensive report on the composition of foods and beverages designed to meet the energy expenditure needs of individuals engaged in intense muscular efforts, emphasizing the importance of proper nutrition in athletic training and performance.\",2\r\n7864,SODIUM INTAKE,\"The event of sodium intake recommendations is discussed, particularly in relation to hypertension.\",2\r\n959,FERRER SVODODA C,Ferrer Svododa C is an author who wrote about hygiene and food safety standards in clinical nutrition.,1\r\n7787,UL,\"The Tolerable Upper Intake Level (UL) refers to the maximum daily intake of a nutrient that is unlikely to cause adverse health effects in the general population. This concept is crucial for understanding safe consumption levels of various nutrients, as exceeding the UL may lead to negative health outcomes. The term UL is consistently used to denote these maximum intake levels, emphasizing the importance of adhering to these guidelines to maintain health and prevent toxicity.\",3\r\n16063,REGLAMENTO (UE) Nº 1924/2006,Reglamento (UE) Nº 1924/2006 establece las normas sobre declaraciones nutricionales y de propiedades saludables en los alimentos.,4\r\n7907,ETIQUETADO NUTRICIONAL,\"The entity \"\"ETIQUETADO NUTRICIONAL\"\" refers to nutritional labeling, which encompasses the regulations and information presented on food packaging. This labeling is designed to inform consumers about the nutritional content of food products, helping them make informed dietary choices.\",4\r\n7788,EAR,\"The t